      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Further investigation seems that this mostly seems to affect one avatar in particular. Others move mostly as I would expect from stable.\n\nI will come back comparing this avatar between stable and ik-beta to see if there is any difference.\n\nMy bonus feature request still stands though, I still prefer the old dumber elbow pre-IK 2.0 IK in certain cases, since you can puppeteer more freely with it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-07-30T06:18:15.634Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I feel like my elbows move way too little without elbow trackers. I think it was almost the case in the previous version, but it is even more noticeable now in the IK beta to the point that I can no longer ignore it. My arms feel like they are glued to my body.\n\nI'd rather have them move more with the risk of clipping than what it does now, because it feels pretty off now to my actual elbow movements.\n\nIf I may also put in a feature request: I've long wished there was an option to restore elbow position being locked more directly to controller position as prior to IK 2.0. While that has the clipping issues (and then perhaps not suitable as a default), it does give you more control and more expressiveness if you puppeteer with this behaviour in mind.",
